lue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, um.<br /> Depending on how pendantic you are with the naming, you already have it in your hands, or you will never see it, because the 20th editions are literally the '4th edition' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What WW is working on is the 5th. &quot;V5&quot;, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is me being pedantic...although I guess in a different way then what you're thinking.<br /> <br /> Wraith and Changeling never got a Revised/3rd edition the same way Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage did. No I don't count the original Orpheus to be Wraith Revised. So Wr20 and C20 are technically their gameline's 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> Ergo, if a new version were to be released for WoD5th, they would in fact be on their 4th edition.<br /> <br /> Similar to how, if we were to assume no 20th anniversary edition is coming for them, if the next edition for Hunter, Mummy, and Demon were to be released for WoD5th, they would technically be on their 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBlack83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1184170-wraith20-backer-pdf-live?p=1184229#post1184229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to purchase this 'raw' backer PDF? Wraith is the one 20th Edition I couldn't afford to back and I really don't want to wait another year for the general one to come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately no.<br /> <br /> Sorry ma